OWNER RULING, 2026-08-27: "even if adr-16 ultimately conveys the correct message
on careful reading, readers do not always read carefully! ... the solution is
NOT to explain the disinfo at length, the solution is to ELIMINATE THOSE WORDS."

AGENTS.md already required this -- "excise-the-superseded-BODY (don't leave
stale text behind a missable banner)" -- so this is drift from a written rule.
Git history is the record; the document should carry one claim, not a claim and
its refutation at equal weight.

THREE EXCISIONS.

ADR-0016 "Why static analysis can answer this" opened with a paragraph
asserting that all I/O transitively reaches stdlib primitives ("requests.get()
eventually calls socket.send()"), followed by "#### Amendment (INV-fotav)"
refuting it. The wrong paragraph was the first thing a reader met. Deleted; the
section now states the correct argument once -- hypergumbo analyses the target
repository, not its dependencies, with the measured zero-net_send-chains result
-- and re-supports "finite and stable" on the responsibility bound rather than
on the deleted transitivity claim.

ADR-0016 module_completeness carried "*This paragraph originally recorded the
opposite* ... That reasoning was sound about the POWER of the grant and wrong
about WHO MAY EXERCISE IT". Deleted; the ruling and its two bounds stand alone.

ADR-0046 Consequences carried MY OWN instance, added earlier the same day: the
original prediction kept, with "the reason is not the one predicted here"
underneath. Deleted; the consequence now states the measured result (33.9% ->
24.1%, all of it KIND-MISDECLARED, CONFIGURED-ACTION zero) and what follows for
cohort design.

ADR-0047's Context quoted the sentence deleted from ADR-0016 and now cites what
the document actually says. No other reference to the removed text exists in the
tree (grep for "transitivity" is clean).

ALSO IN THIS COMMIT: ADR-0047 (Proposed) -- catalogue scope, and where a user's
catalogue data lives. Ten rulings covering the stdlib-scope amendment, seed-not-
copy, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME homes, explicit materialization, provenance and
staleness, three-state disclosure, registry-answers-extensibility, per-language
scope gates, the repo tier, and which of the eight YAML families get a user
channel. Its first Negative states what it does NOT buy back: hypergumbo still
ships and must maintain the third-party rows.

Filed WI-fubom for the sweep: 18 candidate sites across 14 of 49 ADRs, with the
note that most "**Amendment" markers are legitimate additions and only kept
superseded text is the defect.

